From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ASRock-Rack <support@asrockrack.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] group-ext: use ctx->group for response echo byte
Upstream-Status: Pending

Allow group extension handlers to override the response group byte by
modifying request->ctx->group before returning. The framework previously
hard-coded the echo from the raw request byte, making it impossible for
a handler to respond with a different group identifier.

This is needed for the AMI MegaRAC Redfish Host Interface compatibility:
the host BIOS sends NetFn 0x2C with group byte 0x00 but expects the
response to contain group byte 0x52 (DMTF Redfish 'R'). The stock AMI
firmware hard-codes 0x52 in the response regardless of the request.

Existing handlers that do not modify ctx->group are unaffected because
executeIpmiGroupCommand() sets ctx->group from the request byte before
dispatching.

Signed-off-by: ASRock-Rack <support@asrockrack.com>
---
 ipmid-new.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ipmid-new.cpp b/ipmid-new.cpp
index 44890aba..abcdef01 100644
--- a/ipmid-new.cpp
+++ b/ipmid-new.cpp
@@ -304,7 +304,7 @@ message::Response::ptr executeIpmiGroupCommand(message::Request::ptr request)
     message::Response::ptr response =
         executeIpmiCommandCommon(groupHandlerMap, group, request);
     ipmi::message::Payload prefix;
-    prefix.pack(bytes);
+    prefix.pack(static_cast<uint8_t>(request->ctx->group));
     response->prepend(prefix);
     return response;
 }
